 "response": "**Kribun's budget is now $3216K.**\n\nOnly Finance Office records count. PMO, vendor, sales, engineering, legal, marketing, facilities and operations messages are ignored. Finance notes that don't change the amount (audit notes, purchase orders, reminders, cost-centre codes) don't affect the figure either.\n\n**How withdrawals were handled.** Each chain of withdrawals was traced from its last link backward. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect. So an odd number of effective withdrawals removes the original update, and an even number restores it.\n\nSome decisive chains:\n- **#0003 (\u2212$247K) applies.** The chain #0006 \u2192 #0008 \u2192 \u2026 \u2192 #0115 \u2192 #0322 ends at #1291, which is not withdrawn.\n- **#0026 (\u2212$478K) is removed.** #0810 cancels #0104, so #0070 stands.\n- **#0069 (+$67K) is removed.** #1224 cancels #1070, so #0146 stands, #0132 falls, and #0074 stands.\n- **Also removed:**\n  - #0318 (\u2212$219K), via #1523 \u2192 #1125 \u2192 #1123.\n  - #0946 (+$271K), via #1347 \u2192 #1280 \u2192 #1202.\n- **Also applying:**\n  - #0228 (\u2212$577K), via #1586 \u2192 #1545 \u2192 #0962 \u2192 #0608.\n  - #0105 (\u2212$516K), via #1037 \u2192 \u2026 \u2192 #0109.\n  - #0912 (+$596K), via #1578 \u2192 #1478.\n\n**Calculation.** The starting value is $2520K, set by #0001. Every Finance Office change that remains effective was then applied once, in record order. The running total ends at $3216K after #1597 (\u2212$60K). I did this in a single pass and did not run a separate re-check.\n\nANSWER: $3216K",
